            <div xml:id="d394">

                <pb facs="0439" n="339" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg339"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">834.156/66</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Mooney</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Asuncion</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-12-27"><hi rendition="#italic">December 27,
                        1919</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received February 3, 1920.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 561</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my despatch No. 556 of
                    December 24th,<anchor n="19" xml:id="d394-f1"/> I have the honor to inform you,
                    that in my initial interview with Doctor Ramón Lara Castro, the new Paraguayan
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs, I made mention of the pending port concession,
                    whereupon he suggested that I write a formal note setting the matter forth
                    succinctly in accordance with my understanding of it. In accordance with that
                    suggestion I have prepared and transmitted a note on the subject, a copy of
                    which I enclose for your information.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Daniel F. Mooney</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d394-a1.xml" xpointer="d394-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
